    "created_at": "2026-09-13T04:27:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-13T04:27:49Z",
    "body": "End-to-end confirmation on Intel Arc Pro B70 (XPU) that this PR fixes a user-visible failure, with and without speculative decoding.\n\n**Model**: Qwen3.5-4B W4A16 (RedHatAI, GDN hybrid), one B70, `--dtype float16 --quantization compressed-tensors`, greedy. **Harness**: 30 repeats of a completion per prompt length, \"degenerate\" = a single-character wall in the output (from bosd's harness in steveseguin/b70-optimization-lab PR #47).\n\n| runtime | one-token prompt `Hi` | 2, 3, 5, 6, 11-token prompts |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| our served build on 0.27.2rc1.dev77, MTP depth 3 | **30/30 degenerate** (`!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!`) | 0/30 |\n| stock v0.29.0 + our overlays, MTP depth 3 | 29-30/30 | 0/30 |\n| same, no speculation | 29/30 | 0/30 |\n| same **+ only this PR's `gdn_attn.py` hunks** (head 53995de), MTP depth 3 | **0/30** | 0/30 |\n| same + this PR, no speculation | **0/30** | 0/30 |\n\nSo a fresh one-token prefill on a GDN model produces garbage on XPU today, and this PR's first-chunk classification fix removes it. Our lossless gates (three strict pairs on the 4B, 9B and 27B lanes) are being re-run on the patched build now; nothing else changed in the outputs of longer prompts. The earlier same-base CPU regression results in this thread came from our source-level review; this is the runtime confirmation.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
